From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Faris Benhaddou <farisbenhaddou@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:00:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Shader split: Scimitar .forge archives and raw control
 sections off 4-byte boundaries

Assassin's Creed: The Ezio Collection keeps its shaders in Ubisoft's Scimitar
.forge files (Oodle Leviathan / Mermaid entries), which the split did not read,
so AC II's title screen and menus drew nothing. dm/gfx/tools/forge.py reads the
archive tables and the control sections in a decoded block; shader_split.py
scans every entry with the game's own Oodle decoder (forge_jobs,
forge_shaders), profile_guess.py detects the files, and the NSP build passes
oodle_forge. raw_shaders now also takes a main's control sections that start
off a 4-byte boundary when their length is a control section's (164 of AC's
232), and forge material templates get the single-stage pixel-input cover.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: Assassin's Creed: The Ezio Collection's shaders live in Scimitar .forge archives the shader split did not read (its title screen and menus drew nothing)
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#483
